# ENVARC:Sys/timezone - the local time, as a POSIX TZ rule, which
# C:net/TimeSync sets the clock by: the zone's name and its offset west
# of UTC, then the summer zone and when it starts and ends. The first line
# that is not a comment is the rule; without one the clock keeps UTC.
#
#   CET-1CEST,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3     Central Europe (Berlin, Paris, Rome)
#   GMT0BST,M3.5.0/1,M10.5.0       United Kingdom
#   EST5EDT,M3.2.0,M11.1.0         US Eastern
#   PST8PDT,M3.2.0,M11.1.0         US Pacific
#   JST-9                          Japan
#   UTC0                           UTC
CET-1CEST,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3
